guamp: render pass attachments pass their resolve target to the runtime (multisampled passes resolved: Maps' empty map)

2ff4be9's renderCommandEncoderWithDescriptor: never read an attachment's resolveTexture: NmbPassAttachment had no field for it, so a
MultisampleResolve / StoreAndMultisampleResolve store resolved into nothing and the single-sample target the app shows stayed as it
was. VectorKit renders the map multisampled (ggl's texture creation sets sampleCount and private storage for it) and showed an empty
map (fin43); any other multisampled pass did the same. The metal2vulkan runtime resolves (RenderPassAttachment resolve_texture,
resolve_level/slice/depth_plane): NmbPassAttachment gains those four fields (C and Rust, same build) and the frontend fills them, the
resolve texture kept alive with the command buffer and, over an IOSurface, flushed and invalidated as a written surface (0010).
This keeps multisampling, unlike UniXNU/AdrenoMetal 5a50581 (every client single-sample). Rust bridge checked with cargo check on
metal2vulkan 720ef1c; the Objective-C++ is not compiled outside the CI. Applies after 0001-0003, 0009-0014.

